      "comment": "Accessibility label for a puzzle square on a variant board: the square's position, then the rule it sits under, as ONE utterance VoiceOver reads on every focus move. %1$@ is like \"Row 3, column 5\"; %2$@ is like \"cage of 15\" or \"thermometer, 2 of 4\". Both halves are finished translated strings — the comma and space between them is the join, and where a join goes differs per language (Japanese uses 、 and no space). Keep it SHORT: it is spoken every time focus moves.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "%1$@, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "en": {
